[COMMENTS]
STATION,Flat-V weir on the River Ness in a rural catchment. GENERAL: Flat-V weir, 12m wide. Station added to peak flows dataset in August 2021 (WINFAP Files v10). STATION HYDROMETRY: Flat V weir subject to drowning below QMED, some out of bank flow but no by-passing. Theoretical rating amended by hydraulic modelling to cover non-modular flow range. One peak flow rating across period of record. FLOW RECORD: June 2005 peak estimated at 75 cumecs using hydraulic model. FLOW REGIME: Significant groundwater abstractions.
CATCHMENT,Geology: Jurassic Limestone, clays and sandstones. Predominantly rural catchment with moorland headwaters and arable in lower valleys.
Qmed Suitability,Well gauged to QMED.
Pooling Suitability,Gauged close to AMAX1 and high flow rating supported by hydraulic modelling.
[END]
